Keep doing what you've been doing 'till now.  Explore carefully and
retreat when
you need to.  I would continue at least until Medusa's level (you've
got another
5-6 levels), then decide if I could go farther, or just keep to "upper
levels" until
making level 14.  You have plenty of food, so this isn't much of a
problem.

Some advice (spoilers, so you might not want to read on).

Engrave 'Elbereth' with Magicbane often.  This exercises wisdom, take
only one turn and can save your life.  Engrave it on every downstairs.

Engrave it under piles of rocks (So you know where it is).  This will
create barriers that most monsters won't pass.

Bless the potion of gain ability and quaff it.  This will raise all
your
stats by one.  (Less spell failure).

Confused reading of scroll of charging will take your spellpoints to
max (and increase it by 10-15 if at max).

You want to make sure to get a full set of intrinsics, esp. since you
don't have reflection.  Lack of sleep resistance for example can lead
to a YASD.  Try eating the right corpses.

Are you carrying a lizard corpse?

Can you wear a helmet and still cast spells without much failure?  A
dwarven helm (hard hat) can increase your ac by 2.  If not, try a
leather helmet.  (Or try blessed gain ability)

You can try to find more money for protection by digging out
vaults.  Look for "ad aerium" engraved on the ground for a hint
that a vault exists in that level.  Other ways include the spell
of detect treasure, potions of detect objects, and telepathy
(if a monster is created in the vault).

Finally, try to get to level 14 ASAP.  If you have  a single potion of
gain level, get to level 13 then drink it immediatly.  The Wizard Quest
isn't too dangerous, and the quest artifact is one of the best.
Good Luck.

